ISSUE #1214: Can't create a Card on an account using stripe.accounts.createExternalAccount 
Author: LiveLikeCounter
Date: 2021-08-11T12:33:08Z
Labels: 
State: closed

[c0]
Node version: v12.21.0
Stripe node version: ^8.168.0

I want to create a debit-card on Connected Account, but it fails with this error: 
`Error: Requests made on behalf of a connected account must use card tokens from Stripe.js, but card details were directly provided.`

My request for the card I used is:
```
  const card = await stripe.accounts.createExternalAccount(
    "acct_1JNFtC2V9PyKrLnu",
    {
      external_account: {
        object: "card",
        number: "12345678901234567890",
        exp_month: 12,
        exp_year: 21,
      },
    }
  );
```

As far as I read from the doc, I provided the correct information: https://stripe.com/docs/api/external_account_cards/create

When I add a bank account, with the following object, it went fine (of course I used a real bankaccount instead of the 1111111):
```
  const card = await stripe.accounts.createExternalAccount(
    "acct_1JNFtC2V9PyKrLnu",
    {
      external_account: {
        object: "bank_account",
        country: "US",
        currency: "usd",
        routing_number: "111111111",
        account_number: "1111111111",
      },
    }
  );
```

Any thoughts?


--- COMMENTS ---
[c1] @remi-stripe 2021-08-11T14:45:02Z:
@LiveLikeCounter Github issues should be limited to bugs with the library itself. This is more an integration question and we recommend contacting our [support team](https://support.stripe.com/contact) or joining our Discord server to talk to other developers: https://stripe.com/go/developer-chat

To unblock you thought: sending raw card details via the API puts you under a higher level of [PCI compliance](https://stripe.com/docs/security/guide#validating-pci-compliance) and it's banned by default for Connect. You need to collect card details client-side and [create a Token](https://stripe.com/docs/js/tokens_sources/create_token?type=cardElement) (tok_123) for that card and then server-side you send `external_account: 'tok_123'`. 
