[c5] @remi-stripe 2021-09-30T04:08:15Z:
@theredcat the large clients are even more reasons not to retry automatically or provide that option in my opinion. Rate limits are something you need to handle carefully and how to handle them depends on your own approach and business models and a "permanent retry" for all your requests is likely a bad idea. We implement various logic in rate limiting, dropping reads before writes for example and prioritizing some requests over others internally and most advanced/large users should do the same on their end when they start hitting rate limits, on top of alerting for it.
